"<p>Because every stored secret in Nitrobase (SSH keys, server passwords, app env vars, database credentials, backup destination keys, cloud sync tokens, and notification secrets) is encrypted with <code>ENCRYPTION_KEY</code>, changing <code>.env</code> directly without migrating the database would render stored secrets unreadable.</p>\n<p>Use the bundled <code>scripts/rotate-encryption-key.ts</code> script to re-encrypt all database secrets atomically.</p>\n<h2>Rotation Procedure</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Generate a new 32-byte key</strong> (save it in your password manager):</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">openssl</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> rand</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -hex</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 32</span></span></code></pre>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Stop the panel container</strong> so no writes occur during rotation:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">cd</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> /opt/nitrobase</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">docker</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> compose</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -f</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> docker-compose.prod.yml</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> stop</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> app</span></span></code></pre>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Run the key rotation script</strong> with <code>OLD_ENCRYPTION_KEY</code> set to your current key and <code>ENCRYPTION_KEY</code> set to the new key:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">docker</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> compose</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -f</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> docker-compose.prod.yml</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> run</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> --rm</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> \\</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">  -e</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> OLD_ENCRYPTION_KEY='&#x3C;current-key>'</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> \\</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">  -e</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> ENCRYPTION_KEY='&#x3C;new-key>'</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> \\</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">  app</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> bun</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> scripts/rotate-encryption-key.ts</span></span></code></pre>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Update <code>.env</code>:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Replace <code>ENCRYPTION_KEY</code> with the new key.</li>\n<li>Add the old key to <code>ENCRYPTION_KEY_PREVIOUS</code> (comma-separated, newest first) so app backups (<code>env.enc</code>) created before the rotation can still be decrypted and restored until they age out:\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">ENCRYPTION_KEY</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"&#x3C;new-key>\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">ENCRYPTION_KEY_PREVIOUS</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"&#x3C;current-key>\"</span></span></code></pre>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Start the panel again:</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">docker</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> compose</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -f</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> docker-compose.prod.yml</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> up</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -d</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> app</span></span></code></pre>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"docCallout docCallout-note\"><div class=\"docCalloutHeader\"><span class=\"docCalloutBadge\">NOTE</span><span class=\"docCalloutTitle\">Older Self-Backups</span></div><div class=\"docCalloutContent\">\n<p>Self-backup archives (<code>.tar.gz.enc</code>) taken before rotation remain encrypted with the old key. When decrypting an older self-backup manually with <code>openssl</code> or via First-Run Restore, supply the key that was active when that backup was created.</p>\n</div></div>"